32 bits: the semicolons of the 32-bit branches.

Their int builtins miss them where ARCH_SIXTYFOUR is not defined, which
the 64-bit hosts never compile.

--- a/utils/int_builtins_c.c
+++ b/utils/int_builtins_c.c
@@
-    return __builtin_ffs(v)
+    return __builtin_ffs(v);
@@
-    return __builtin_ctz(v)
+    return __builtin_ctz(v);
@@
-    return __builtin_popcount(v)
+    return __builtin_popcount(v);
